<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine judge says airport privatization void.</title>
<headline>Argentine judge says airport privatization void.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>A federal Argentine judge ruled Tuesday that President Carlos Menem's decree to privatize the country's airports is void, the judge's office said.</p>
<p>Menem decreed the privatization of most of the country's main airports June 2, in a tender for a single, 30-year concession to be awarded in October.  </p>
<p>An official in the office of Judge Liliana Heiland told Reuters that she wrote in her ruling: &quot;The system implemented in the decree 375/97, which regulates the matter, manifestly exceeds the executive's powers.&quot;</p>
<p>Heiland was ruling on a court case brought by opposition politicians.</p>
<p>No government official was available immediately for comment.</p>
<p>((--Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
